cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the
  references listed in this file (Silva 2003, for the original transit model,
  and Duque Estrada, Pinho & Valio 2025, for the Python implementation).
  For works in Portuguese or published in Brazil, please also cite
  Duque Estrada, Pinho & Valio 2026 (Revista Brasileira de Ensino de Fisica).
title: "Pipeline MCMC: ECLIPSE planetary transit model with MCMC fitting"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Beatriz
    family-names: Duque Estrada
    affiliation: "CRAAM, Universidade Presbiteriana Mackenzie"
  - given-names: Felipe
    family-names: Pinho
    affiliation: "CRAAM, Universidade Presbiteriana Mackenzie"
  - given-names: Adriana
    family-names: Valio
    affiliation: "CRAAM, Universidade Presbiteriana Mackenzie"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Transit-Model-CRAAM/pipelineMCMC"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  Python/C code to compute the light curve of a star with transiting exoplanets, including starspots and faculae (ECLIPSE model), with parallelized MCMC fitting of the transit parameters.
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - planetary transits
  - starspots
  - stellar activity
  - light curves
  - MCMC
